---
import RoomLayout from '../layouts/RoomLayout.astro';
---
<RoomLayout title="SHIP — legal & privacy" description="Ship is local-first: your data stays on your machine. Beta terms + security contact.">
  <div class="room-card wide legal">
    <div class="room-eyebrow">Legal · Public beta</div>
    <h1 class="room-title">The short version.</h1>
    <p class="room-lede">Full terms land before general availability. During public beta, here's the honest summary — no dark patterns, no surprises.</p>

    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>Ship is <b>local-first</b>. Your prompts, data, collections, and artifacts stay on your machine — we don't collect or transmit them. The only thing we store is the email you give us for the waitlist, used solely to tell you when installers land. Bring-your-own-model means your model provider's terms govern what you send them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Terms</h2>
      <p>Ship is <b>free for personal use</b> during public beta and provided as-is while we stabilise it. A paid cloud-side tier will follow — pricing isn't locked yet and we'll publish the terms here before charging anyone. Your local Ship keeps working either way.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>Agents are <b>scoped by default</b>: filesystem, shell, and network access are explicit per agent, privileged actions wait for your approval, and everything is audited. Found something? Email <a href="mailto:security@getship.dev">security@getship.dev</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="room-switch"><a href="/">← Back to the desktop</a></div>
  </div>
</RoomLayout>

<style>
  .legal { text-align: left; }
  .legal .room-eyebrow, .legal .room-title, .legal .room-lede { align-self: flex-start; }
  .legal .room-title, .legal .room-lede { text-align: left; }
  .sec { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; }
  .sec h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0; color: var(--foreground); }
  .sec p { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--foreground) 72%, var(--background)); }
  .sec p b { color: var(--foreground); font-weight: 600; }
  .sec a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .room-switch { align-self: flex-start; }
</style>
